{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014To21xBiMfjAauuSFuoaJt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor â€” what it is:**\n\n- **A personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty** â€” a single-folder app (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`, no OneDrive/syncing) that turns plain markdown files into a live task-and-project dashboard. The markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`) are the source of truth; there's no database.\n\n- **Ships as a self-contained local web app.** `anchor_gui.py` is a Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders the dashboard and writes back to the markdown directly. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` on `http://localhost:8777`. `anchor.py` is a CLI mirror of the same logic that also generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Core task workflow:** capture/add tasks with priorityÂ·energyÂ·domainÂ·dueÂ·notes, check them done, and move them through a lifecycle (Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored), all editable inline in the browser and logged to daily `logs/`.\n\n- **Self-tests itself daily.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler â€” it parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server on a test port, exercises every endpoint and task state, and writes a dated report to `health_reports/`.\n\n- **Its major engineering investment is an \"R&D control surface\" layered on top** â€” a per-project cockpit for running the *trio* (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) as durable, server-side AI sessions. Built across four versions:\n  - **v2:** session model + cached/validated summaries + Grass-Catchers idea lane + deliverable pinning + an interactive stream-json REPL terminal.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\":** real ConPTY terminals (the one declared native dep, `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, in-place expandable summaries, runnable deliverable previews (port always â‰  8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built, 9 waves GREEN, 637 passed, merged to master): lane tiles with one honest status light, inline expanding panels (summary-on-top / resizable xterm terminal below), a skill that auto-loads/greets exactly **once** (kills the repeating-prompt bug), a claudeâ†”gemini engine toggle, per-lane doc roles, a cost/tokens/time rollup, grassâ†’lane promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Hard constraint it holds to:** Python stdlib only, with the single declared exception of `pywinpty` for the terminal subsystem (optional, lazy-imported, degrades gracefully); `distro.py`'s import scan enforces this. Everything stays plain-text and accessible from any CLI tool.\n\nOne note on grounding: the **current branch is `foreman/rnd-v4.1-cockpit`** with uncommitted changes and untracked `.anchor/` and `rnd_jobs/` dirs â€” so there appears to be a **v4.1 cockpit iteration in progress** beyond the merged v4 described above. The bullets above reflect what the committed docs claim; the working tree shows active follow-on work."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c5f99dc2-b7bc-4584-bd68-817288bbb61c","uuid":"feadb795-6d60-4e2b-96ef-80b4e3a7b8e3","request_id":"req_011Cc2F8CN9vaTFQ74d6xdN1"}
